[COMMENTS]
STATION,A non-standard flume structure located in the upper catchment of the River Gade, a tributary of the River Colne. GENERAL: A non-standard rectangular flume with side contractions installed by Hemel Hempstead Development Corporation in the mid 1960s. The station was operated by the local authority until the mid 1970s when its operation passed to Thames Water and subsequently the Environment Agency. Used for both Water Resource and Flood Incident management. STATION HYDROMETRY: The original instrumentation was a Lea Integrating recorder and early records were of poor quality. Lea Recorder replaced in Jan 1978 by the more accurate Munro Recorder. One rating applied across period of record. Rating has tendency to overestimate low flows, peak flows show good agreement with calibration gaugings. Stage at Q95 lower than recommended for a flume structure. A large fall at the end of the structure ensures modular conditions throughout. Before Jan 1978, peaks were attenuated by use of upstream automatic sluice gate which passed flow into storage pond. FLOW RECORD: Upstream channel through park is perched, through periods of high groundwater levels and high rainfall events the river will overtop into the park. Upstream trash screen prone to blockage and can also cause out of bank flow. Some gaps in data caused by vandalism of recording hut. Springflow is culverted through the park and enters the river downstream of the gauging station. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14). FLOW REGIME: Baseflow-dominated regime with significant artificial disturbance. The urban response runoff has a significant effect on flood peaks. Balancing ponds u/s within built-up area.
CATCHMENT,Dip-slope stream draining the Chilterns. The solid geology is Chalk with some tertiary and extensive boulder clay cover. A mainly rural catchment draining to Hemel Hempstead (part of which is u/s of the station).
Qmed Suitability,Gauged above QMED. Good fit to gaugings.
Pooling Suitability,Well gauged above QMED. However, rating does tend to underestimate high flows.
[END]
